{
  "_what_this_is": "A reading of catalogue_stills.json — the record whose BLANK verdicts Builder 1 retracted and whose MEASURED verdicts I was asked to treat as evidence. Read from the artefact on lane/agentic-builder2, not from either lane's description of it.",
  "_the_first_correction": "IT IS NOT A PIXEL DIFF. Every row compares `bytes` against `empty_control_bytes` — PNG FILE LENGTH. No pixel is read anywhere in the record. Both lanes called it a pixel diff, which is how it came to be trusted as a verdict: a length cannot say WHERE something drew, and cannot tell a component that drew the RIGHT thing from one that drew the wrong thing at the same size.",
  "_the_second_correction": "THE CONTROL IS NOT ONE CONTROL. 11 rows share control 37837; six have none at all (-1, honestly reported CONTROL_ABSENT); the remaining 12 each carry a control unique to themselves. A per-component control is defensible — it may be the component's own canvas — but it means the 7 BLANKs are not one finding.",
  "_the_blank_split": "Of the 7 BLANK rows, ALL have still == control byte for byte. Three (EndCard, MouseDrag, SpeechBubble) compare against the SHARED empty control, which is what a component drawing nothing actually looks like. Four (RecordingFrame, Reticle, Timeline, TimelineRoadmap) compare against a control unique to themselves AND equal to themselves — undecidable between 'drew nothing on its own canvas' and 'the comparison read one file twice'. Comparing a thing with itself is a HARNESS FAULT, never a zero, and nothing in this record separates the two.",
  "_why_it_still_supports_BYTES_ONLY": "The five MEASURED rows this lane carries run 3.0x-4.7x the shared control's length (+74k to +140k bytes). A PNG that encodes to four times the length of the empty frame contains a great deal more than the empty frame, so SOMETHING rendered. That is real evidence and weaker evidence at once — which is exactly why it is named BYTES_ONLY and does not reach the menu.",
  "shared_control_bytes": 37837,
